<title>GERMANY: E.German Aug industry output rises 5.1 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E.German Aug industry output rises 5.1 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Aug 96    July 96	Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +5.1	-5.7	  +8.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year			unch	+3.6	   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     145.1	138.1	  145.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbnk statistics.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Aug 96	    July 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   159.5	 +7.5    148.4	  -8.8</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    192.0	 +3.9    184.8	  -0.2</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   136.3	+14.2    119.4	 -18.7</p>
<p> Energy output	     88.8	 -1.1     89.8	  -0.2</p>
<p> Construction	     207.4	 +4.1    199.3	  -2.4</p>
<p>Two month comparison July/Aug 96 with May/June 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			  -2.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison July/Aug 96 with July/Aug 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			  +1.6</p>
<p> Mining					 -4.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		    +5.4</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	  +7.1</p>
<p>		Capital goods		 +0.6</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	   -6.0</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	     +11.6</p>
<p> Energy output				+3.1</p>
<p> Construction				 -4.0</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-2609750</p>
